content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-107 - AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22950",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end vibration is 5.5 mm/s RMS, up from 3.0 last month. The applicable limit is the HF-300 vibration severity chart (Figure 3). 5.5 falls in Zone C (4.5 to 7.1 mm/s), 'Restricted - plan maintenance'. It is below the 7.1 mm/s Zone D boundary, where the instruction is 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. Last month's 3.0 was in Zone B (2.8 to 4.5, long-term operation), so the reading has moved up one zone in a month.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The manual says to measure both bearing housings weekly and to classify the highest reading using Figure 3. Only the drive-end reading is reported. The zone classification therefore rests on the DE value until a non-drive-end reading is confirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end housing temperature is 76 C. The applicable limits are in the manual specification table: normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C. The reading is 6 C above normal and 4 C below the alarm limit. Temperatures are measured on the housing surface.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage is reported at the shaft seal, so the seal leakage symptom does not apply. No seal replacement is triggered by this report.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing wear (most likely). Bearing wear is listed as a cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature. Here both symptoms are present at the same drive-end housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. Misalignment is also listed as a cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing of the drive-end bearing. This is listed as a cause of high bearing temperature, though it does not by itself explain the vibration rise.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage. This is listed as a cause of high vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation (insufficient NPSH). This is listed as a cause of high vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before shutdown, take vibration readings on both bearing housings (DE and NDE). Classify the highest reading against Figure 3. If any reading reaches 7.1 mm/s RMS or more (Zone D), stop the pump immediately.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Until the repair is done, monitor DE housing temperature against the limits: alarm at 80 C, trip at 90 C. Escalate to an immediate stop if the alarm is reached.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check NPSH and suction conditions for cavitation.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check grease quantity in the bearings for over-greasing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Plan a shutdown. Isolate and drain the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly using lifting equipment, because the assembly mass is 68 kg. Inspect the bearings and the impeller for wear, imbalance or damage.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair: DE HF3-512 (6312-C3) and NDE HF3-510 (6310-C3).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the seal has to be disturbed, fit cartridge seal HF3-450B, not HF3-450, because this pump is serial HF3-22000 or above. HF3-450B is pre-set and needs no sleeve measurement. Tighten the HF3-450B gland nut to 30 Nm. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120 on reassembly; it must be replaced whenever the casing is opened. Tighten the remaining fasteners to manual Table 5. Table 5 values are not available in the evidence (see open questions).",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or the bearing housing, re-align with the laser alignment tool to 0.05 mm parallel and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, re-measure vibration on both bearing housings and confirm the reading is back in Zone A or B. Confirm the DE temperature is 70 C or below.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3 (replace as a pair if worn)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 (replace as a pair if worn)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (replace whenever casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before opening it.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Lifting equipment is required for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump if vibration reaches Zone D (7.1 mm/s RMS or more) or the bearing temperature reaches the 80 C alarm or 90 C trip.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The seal must never run dry. Confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from the pump discharge is established before and during restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 hours, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 hours, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement, only if the seal must be disturbed: 4.0 hours, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual (AQ-OM-300 Rev D) lists the mechanical seal as HF3-450, component type, fitted per section 5.2 with fasteners to Table 5. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes this for HF-300 pumps with serial HF3-22000 and above: use cartridge seal HF3-450B with a gland nut torque of 30 Nm (previously 25 Nm). P-107 is serial HF3-22950, which is at or above HF3-22000. The bulletin therefore applies: do not fit HF3-450, and use HF3-450B at 30 Nm if the seal is disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Figure 3 does not say which zone a value exactly on a boundary belongs to. This does not affect P-107, because 5.5 mm/s is clearly inside Zone C.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Table 5 fastener torque values (casing, impeller nut, bearing housing) are not included in the evidence and must be obtained from the full manual.",
    "No non-drive-end vibration or temperature reading was reported; the manual requires both housings to be measured.",
    "Grease type, quantity and relubrication interval are not given in the evidence.",
    "The evidence does not state whether bearing replacement requires removing the mechanical seal. This determines whether HF3-450B should be pre-ordered.",
    "No detailed bearing replacement procedure beyond 'replace both as a pair' is provided.",
    "The evidence gives no lockout/permit, PPE or site-specific isolation requirements beyond 'isolate and drain'.",
    "No vibration spectrum or phase data is available to distinguish bearing wear from misalignment, imbalance or cavitation.",
    "The required timeframe for completing maintenance in Zone C ('plan maintenance') is not specified."
  ]
}
